From 9e268c3905b975110401991d6c96f34307791fb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:40:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign team member profile: staff photos, drill-down pages,
 PDF/Excel exports

Team member profile page gets a full redesign: staff photo (self-service
upload from the sales dashboard header, admin-editable for anyone from
Admin > Staff, viewable/downloadable/shareable via tap-to-open lightbox),
an on-demand custom date range alongside the existing period chips, and
Dues/Dealers/Orders stat tiles that each open their own back-button detail
page instead of showing everything inline. Item-wise sales becomes
collapsible. Every report (Dues, Dealers, Orders, Item-wise sales) gets
its own PDF and Excel export, reusing the existing exportTableToPdf/
exportRowsToExcel helpers already used elsewhere in the app.

New staff-media storage bucket (public read, write restricted to a
staff member's own folder or an admin, mirroring the dealer-media/
visit-media pattern). Self-service photo changes go through a narrow
update_my_photo() RPC that only ever touches photo_url and re-derives
the caller's identity from auth.uid() server-side, rather than a
blanket "staff can update own row" policy that would let self role
escalation slip in through the same row-level RLS. Admin's photo
change path reuses the existing "admins can update any staff profile"
policy already used for every other field. New get_team_member_orders()
RPC returns the actual order rows the new Orders drill-down needs
(get_team_member_orders_count already existed for the tile's number).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GxWPdEf21EL6SvRpGBbX8q
